@page
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy policy";
}
<div class="container py-4">
    <article class="prose">
        <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
        <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
        <p class="text-muted">Last updated @DateTime.UtcNow.Year.</p>

        <h2>What we store</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Account:</strong> your name, email address, password (stored only as a secure hash), and optionally your phone number, city and a short bio.</li>
            <li><strong>Listings:</strong> the items you publish, including photos you upload.</li>
            <li><strong>Bookings and reviews:</strong> the dates, prices and messages of rentals you request or receive, and reviews you write.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Who can see what</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Your name, city, bio, listings and reviews are public.</li>
            <li>Your email address is shared only with the other person of an <em>accepted</em> booking, so you can arrange pick-up.</li>
            <li>Your phone number is never shown to other users.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Cookies</h2>
        <p>We use a strictly necessary cookie to keep you signed in, and an anti-forgery cookie to protect forms. We don't use tracking or advertising cookies. Your light/dark theme choice is stored in your browser only.</p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>Under the GDPR you can access, download and delete your personal data at any time from <a asp-area="Identity" asp-page="/Account/Manage/PersonalData">Account settings → Personal data</a>.</p>
    </article>
</div>
